---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="About"
  description="Learn about Start Investing Simple's mission to make investing and personal finance easy to understand for beginners."
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6">
    <div class="corner-card mb-10 overflow-hidden rounded-sm">
      <img
        src="/img/about-workspace.jpg"
        alt="A minimal desk workspace with a laptop, representing a calm, focused approach to managing money"
        class="h-64 w-full object-cover sm:h-80"
        loading="eager"
      />
    </div>

    <div class="prose prose-invert max-w-none prose-a:text-brand prose-strong:text-paper">
      <h1>About Start Investing Simple</h1>

      <p>
        Start Investing Simple was created for one reason: investing and personal finance are usually explained
        in a way that assumes you already know the basics. We think that's backwards. Our goal is to break down
        investing, saving, and money management into plain, honest, jargon-free language so anyone — regardless
        of background — can build the confidence to manage their own money.
      </p>

      <h2>Our approach</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Beginner-first.</strong> Every article assumes no prior knowledge and defines terms as we go.</li>
        <li><strong>No hype, no products to sell.</strong> We don't push specific stocks, brokers, or "get rich quick" schemes.</li>
        <li><strong>Educational, not advice.</strong> We explain how things work so you can make informed decisions — we don't tell you what to do with your money. See our <a href="/disclaimer/">disclaimer</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Kept up to date.</strong> We review and update articles as tax rules, contribution limits, and best practices change.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How we make money</h2>
      <p>
        Running a site like this isn't free — hosting, tools, and the time it takes to research and write each
        article all add up. Start Investing Simple is funded through display advertising (like Google AdSense),
        which is why you'll see ads on some pages. That's it — there's no other revenue source right now.
      </p>
      <p>
        We don't accept payment to write about a specific product, and nothing on this site is a sponsored post
        or paid placement. Ads don't influence what we choose to write about or what we say in an article. See our{' '}
        <a href="/privacy-policy/">privacy policy</a> for more on how ads and cookies work on this site.
      </p>

      <h2>Who's behind this</h2>
      <p>
        Start Investing Simple is written and maintained by <strong>Taha Tariq</strong>, a software engineer based
        in London with a background in full-stack development and enterprise systems administration. Professionally,
        Taha spends his time breaking down complex technical systems into clear, workable pieces — and this site
        applies that same instinct to personal finance: taking a subject that's usually explained with unnecessary
        jargon and making it understandable for anyone starting from zero.
      </p>
      <p>
        This site isn't written from the perspective of a licensed financial advisor — it's written from the
        perspective of someone who got interested in investing, found most explanations needlessly confusing, and
        wanted to document the plain-English version he wished he'd had from the start. See our
        <a href="/disclaimer/">disclaimer</a> for more on what that does (and doesn't) mean.
      </p>

      <h2>Questions or feedback?</h2>
      <p>We'd love to hear from you — visit our <a href="/contact/">contact page</a> to get in touch.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
